  "worked_solution": "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(6-x):$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/04dd8257ef32291b930aa29f5bed4de2c41761692fd48d08ed2479f6cbd78659.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(6-x)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Moreover, from the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(6-x)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\frac{7}{\\pi }(\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(6-x))=\\frac{7}{\\pi }\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$",
